{"id":"G2042","lemma":"ἐρεθίζω","transliteration":"erethizō","sayIt":"erethizō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to provoke/irritate","meaning":"ἐρεθίζω\n[in LXX: Dan LXX 11:10, 25 (גָּרָה hithp.), 1Ma.15:40, 2Ma.14:17, etc. ;]\n1. to stir up, provoke (as in cl.): Col.3:21.\n2. In good sense (cf. ἐρεθισμός, excitement, in MGr.), to stir up, stimulate: 2Co.9:2.†\n(AS)","glosses":["most of","provoke"],"count":2,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"2co-9","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"most of","kjv":"ath provoked"}},{"chapterId":"col-3","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"provoke","kjv":"provoke"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"2 Corinthians 9:2","note":"for I know your readiness, of which I boast on your behalf to those of Macedonia, that Achaia has been prepared for the past year. Your zeal has stirred up…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Colossians 3:21","note":"Fathers, don’t provoke your children, so that they won’t be discouraged.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G7499","lemma":"ἐρεθισμός","transliteration":"erethismos","gloss":"aggravation"},{"id":"G20420","lemma":"ἐπικαινίζω","transliteration":"epikainizō","gloss":"to renew"},{"id":"G20421","lemma":"ἐπικάλαμοι","transliteration":"epikalamoi","gloss":"stalk"},{"id":"G20422","lemma":"ἐπικαρπολογέομαι","transliteration":"epikarpologeomai","gloss":"glean"},{"id":"G20423","lemma":"ἐπικαταπνέω","transliteration":"epikatapneō","gloss":"against"},{"id":"G20424","lemma":"ἐπικινέω","transliteration":"epikineō","gloss":"be moved"},{"id":"G20425","lemma":"ἐπίκλησις","transliteration":"epiklēsis","gloss":"appellatio, appeal"},{"id":"G20426","lemma":"ἐπίκοιλος","transliteration":"epikoilos","gloss":"porous, spongy"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}